  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying outcomes with probabilities below 20% and increasing their weight, but neither lottery has such outcomes, so no adjustment would occur. The individual does not refer to any probability transformation or special treatment of rare events. Instead, they treat probabilities as roughly equal and base their choice on the size of the loss. This aligns with a simplification heuristic rather than the specific probability-upweighting rule. The information considered (loss magnitude) and the justification (smaller loss in B) do not match the decision reason’s focus on reweighting low-probability events. Therefore, there is no evidence the individual applied the specified decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
